 "notes": "PDF page 2 of 9, printed 'עמוד 1 מתוך 8' (pageIndex 1; PDF page 1 is the unnumbered instructions cover) of Bituach Leumi form BL/211 (work-injury claim, 05.2015): the claim-type band, section 1 (claimant details) and section 2 (workplace details). Flat Word export with a text layer, no AcroForm; every bound was read from the PDF's own geometry (ruled cell edges, comb tick positions, the Wingdings checkbox glyph squares and the underscore runs, via pdf.js operator list and a raster measurement of the 150 dpi render) and then checked against the render with overlay.mjs. Conventions, copied from the Hebrew truths itc101-page1 and health-page1 and the scanned irs-1040-1970 note: (1) an ID/phone/number tick comb is ONE `comb` target with `cells`, bounded to the cell strip from the baseline up to the regular tick tops (taller separator ticks, e.g. before the check digit or after an area code, are not included); a phone is one 10-cell run because its ticks are continuous. (2) a day/month/year tick comb is ONE `date` target (8 cells, DD MM YYYY), never three, as in itc101; a date on a blank underline is a `date` with no cells. (3) a ruled cell that carries its caption inside, top-right (the name cells, the email cell), is bounded to the writing strip beneath the caption, as in irs-1040-1970; a cell whose caption sits in its own header cell above (the address rows, employer, role, business name and business type) is the whole input cell. (4) a checkbox is the printed square itself (measured ink of the Wingdings glyph, about 10 x 10 pt), not the glyph advance box, as in itc101; option checkboxes are labelled \"option / group caption\" with the verbatim Hebrew caption in logical order. (5) an underscore run is a `text` target bounded from the line up to one text height above it, x from the first to the last underscore. Section-2 captions repeat for the employed block and the self-employed block, so those labels carry a group suffix. Not annotated: the \"לשימוש פנימי בלבד\" office-use boxes (document-type, pages, scan ID comb), the \"חותמת קבלה\" stamp box, the logo, the numbered section badges, the grey section bars and every pre-printed caption.",
